<WovenDocs::Page
  @id="dropdown"
  @title="Dropdown"
  @subtitle="Select-like menu with groups, search, keyboard navigation, remote options and creation."
  @components="Woven::Dropdown, Woven::Autocomplete"
>
  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Overview" @id="overview">
    <p class="woven-doc__intro">
      The default trigger is a
      <code class="wu-code">button.wu-select</code>
      with the kit select look; its menu is the kit
      <code class="wu-code">wu-autocomplete-list</code>. A custom trigger
      gets the kit
      <code class="wu-code">wu-dropdown</code>
      action menu instead. The menu renders into a
      <code class="wu-code">wu-layer</code>
      resolved by the layer service when it opens: the layer of the nearest
      open dialog that contains the trigger, else the body layer, so no
      ancestor can clip it and it stays usable inside a modal or drawer. It is
      mounted only while open, positioned by the anchor modifier against the
      trigger, flips when the preferred side does not fit, follows scroll and
      resize, and dismisses on an outside click or once the trigger leaves
      the viewport. The kit script is not loaded; the
      component owns open state and aria-expanded itself.
    </p>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Features" @id="features">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Grouped options kept contiguous so keyboard order matches visual order.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Type-to-filter search that appears automatically past eight options.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Arrow, Enter, Escape and Tab handling; Escape stops at the menu so a drawer underneath stays open.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Filterable combobox mode, remote search with debounce and stale-result protection, create-on-the-fly.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Icons, danger items, disabled items and separators; custom trigger block and a menu block for your own items.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>onOpen callback to load what the menu shows.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Focus returns to the trigger on close.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Options and value" @id="value">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Controlled, grouped, searchable"
      @note="Ten grouped options: the in-menu search appears because the count passes the threshold of eight. value and onSelect keep the selection in the controller."
      @code={{this.code.controlled}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown
        @options={{this.areaOptions}}
        @value={{this.dropdownValue}}
        @placeholder="Select an area"
        @onSelect={{this.updateDropdown}}
      />
      <span class="wu-text sm muted" data-test-woven-dropdown-value>Value: {{this.dropdownValue}}</span>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Uncontrolled"
      @note="Without value the dropdown remembers its own pick after the first select. onSelect still fires, so a page can react without owning the state."
      @code={{this.code.uncontrolled}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}} @placeholder="Pick a type" @onSelect={{this.notePick}} />
      <span class="wu-text sm muted" data-test-woven-dropdown-pick>Picked: {{this.uncontrolledPick}}</span>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="String options"
      @note="Plain strings are both value and label. Three options stay under the search threshold, so the menu is a simple list."
      @code={{this.code.strings}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}} @placeholder="No search (3 options)" />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Icons and a disabled option"
      @note="Objects may carry an icon glyph before the label; a disabled option is shown but cannot be picked or highlighted."
      @code={{this.code.icons}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.iconOptions}} @placeholder="With icons" />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <h3 class="woven-subtitle">Option shape</h3>
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="args" @rows={{this.optionRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Search" @id="search">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Search suppressed"
      @note="searchable false hides the in-menu search even past the threshold, for action menus where typing makes no sense."
      @code={{this.code.searchableOff}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.areaOptions}} @placeholder="Search suppressed" @searchable={{false}} />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Threshold and placeholder"
      @note="searchThreshold lowers the count at which the search appears; searchPlaceholder labels it. For short lists whose labels are long."
      @code={{this.code.threshold}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown
        @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}}
        @placeholder="Search from 2 options"
        @searchThreshold={{2}}
        @searchPlaceholder="Filter types"
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Placement" @id="placement">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Opens upward"
      @note="placement up prefers the space above the trigger, for controls near the bottom of a page or a drawer footer. It still flips down when there is no room."
      @code={{this.code.up}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.areaOptions}} @placeholder="Opens upward" @placement="up" />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Start edge"
      @note="The menu's start edge meets the trigger's start edge; the default when nothing is set."
      @code={{this.code.placementStart}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}} @placeholder="Menu at start edge" @placement="start" />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="End edge"
      @note="The menu hangs from the trigger's end edge, for a control at the end of a toolbar so the menu stays on screen."
      @code={{this.code.placementEnd}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}} @placeholder="Menu at end edge" @placement="end" />
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Alignment" @id="alignment">
    {{#each this.alignExamples as |example|}}
      <WovenDocs::Example @title={{example.title}} @note={{example.note}} @layout="stack" @code={{example.code}}>
        <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}} @placeholder="Align {{example.align}}" @align={{example.align}} />
      </WovenDocs::Example>
    {{/each}}

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Options alignment"
      @note="optionsAlign aligns the text inside the menu independently of the trigger."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.optionsAlign}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown
        @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}}
        @placeholder="Centered options"
        @align="end"
        @optionsAlign="center"
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Trigger" @id="trigger">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Disabled"
      @note="The trigger renders disabled and the menu never opens."
      @code={{this.code.disabled}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}} @placeholder="Disabled" @disabled={{true}} />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Size"
      @note="size forwards to the trigger button or the filter input, so the dropdown matches neighboring sm controls."
      @code={{this.code.size}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @options={{this.propertyTypeOptions}} @placeholder="Small" @size="sm" />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Custom trigger, action menu"
      @note="The trigger block yields toggle and isOpen for any control. Separators, a disabled item and a danger item make a row action menu."
      @code={{this.code.trigger}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown
        @options={{this.rowActions}}
        @onSelect={{this.runAction}}
        @searchable={{false}}
        @optionsAlign="center"
      >
        <:trigger as |toggle isOpen|>
          <Woven::Button
            @icon="dots-three"
            @shape="square"
            @onClick={{toggle}}
            aria-label="Row actions"
            aria-expanded={{if isOpen "true" "false"}}
            data-test-woven-row-actions
          />
        </:trigger>
      </Woven::Dropdown>
      <span class="wu-text sm muted" data-test-woven-action-result>Last action: {{this.actionResult}}</span>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Menu block and onOpen"
      @note="With a trigger block, the menu block replaces the options with your own items inside the kit wu-dropdown menu and yields close. Give each item wu-dropdown-item and role menuitem or menuitemradio; arrow keys move between them, and a click on one closes the menu after the item's own handlers, so a LinkTo still navigates. onOpen fires each time the menu opens, the place to load what it shows."
      @code={{this.code.menuBlock}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown @onOpen={{this.noteOpen}} data-test-woven-menu-block>
        <:trigger as |toggle isOpen|>
          <Woven::Button
            @text="Sort"
            @onClick={{toggle}}
            class="caret"
            aria-haspopup="menu"
            aria-expanded={{if isOpen "true" "false"}}
            data-test-woven-menu-block-trigger
          />
        </:trigger>
        <:menu as |close|>
          <div role="group" aria-label="Sort">
            {{#each this.sortChoices as |choice|}}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="wu-dropdown-item"
                role="menuitemradio"
                aria-checked={{if (eq this.sortOrder choice.value) "true" "false"}}
                tabindex="-1"
                data-test-woven-menu-block-item={{choice.value}}
                {{on "click" (fn this.pickSort choice.value)}}
              >{{choice.label}}</button>
            {{/each}}
            <hr class="wu-dropdown-separator" />
            <LinkTo @route="woven.index" class="wu-dropdown-item" role="menuitem" tabindex="-1">Overview page</LinkTo>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="wu-dropdown-item"
              role="menuitem"
              tabindex="-1"
              {{on "click" close}}
            >Close</button>
          </div>
        </:menu>
      </Woven::Dropdown>
      <span class="wu-text sm muted" data-test-woven-menu-block-result>Sort: {{this.sortOrder}}, opened {{this.openCount}} times</span>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Combobox modes" @id="combobox">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Filterable"
      @note="The trigger becomes an input; typing filters the options and clearing it calls onClear. For long static lists such as countries."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.filterable}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown
        @filterable={{true}}
        @options={{this.areaOptions}}
        @value={{this.filterValue}}
        @placeholder="Type to filter areas"
        @onSelect={{this.updateFilter}}
        @onClear={{this.clearFilter}}
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Remote search"
      @note="remote takes options from onSearch after minChars and a debounce; promptText and emptyText label the empty menu, selectedLabel shows a value the options no longer contain. The demo resolves after a short delay; a real page fetches."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.remote}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown
        @filterable={{true}}
        @remote={{true}}
        @minChars={{2}}
        @searchDebounce={{250}}
        @promptText="Type two letters"
        @emptyText="No areas match"
        @value={{this.remoteValue}}
        @selectedLabel={{this.remoteLabel}}
        @placeholder="Search areas (remote)"
        @onSearch={{this.searchAreas}}
        @onSelect={{this.selectRemote}}
        @onClear={{this.clearRemote}}
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Create on the fly"
      @note="allowCreate offers an Add row for a term that matches no option; onCreate returns the new option and it becomes the selection."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.create}}
    >
      <Woven::Dropdown
        @filterable={{true}}
        @allowCreate={{true}}
        @options={{this.creatableOptions}}
        @placeholder="Pick or add a type"
        @onCreate={{this.createType}}
        @onSelect={{this.selectCreated}}
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Arguments" @id="arguments">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="args" @rows={{this.argRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Callbacks" @id="callbacks">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="callbacks" @rows={{this.callbackRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Blocks" @id="blocks">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="blocks" @rows={{this.blockRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Autocomplete" @id="autocomplete">
    <p class="woven-note">
      <code>Woven::Autocomplete</code> is a filterable Woven::Dropdown over
      records. It maps each record to
      <code>{ value: record.id, label: record[labelKey] }</code> and reports
      the full record on select. Pass <code>@options</code> to filter a
      preloaded list locally, or <code>@onSearch</code> to fetch matches;
      the host owns transport. In this app,
      <code>RemoteAutocomplete</code> wraps it with URL fetching.
    </p>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Local records"
      @note="Preloaded records filtered as you type; the selected name stays in the input."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.autocompleteLocal}}
    >
      <Woven::Autocomplete
        @options={{this.buildings}}
        @value={{this.buildingId}}
        @selectedName={{this.buildingName}}
        @placeholder="Search buildings"
        @onSelect={{this.pickBuilding}}
        @onClear={{this.clearBuilding}}
        data-test-woven-autocomplete-local
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Remote search with create"
      @note="onSearch resolves records after two characters; onCreate adds an Add row for a name that matches nothing and selects the new record."
      @layout="stack"
      @code={{this.code.autocompleteRemote}}
    >
      <Woven::Autocomplete
        @value={{this.tenantId}}
        @selectedName={{this.tenantName}}
        @placeholder="Search tenants"
        @onSearch={{this.searchTenants}}
        @onCreate={{this.createTenant}}
        @onSelect={{this.pickTenant}}
        @onClear={{this.clearTenant}}
        data-test-woven-autocomplete-remote
      />
      <span class="wu-text sm muted">Selected: {{if this.tenantName this.tenantName "none"}}</span>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <h3 class="woven-subtitle">Autocomplete arguments</h3>
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="args" @rows={{this.autocompleteArgRows}} />
    <h3 class="woven-subtitle">Autocomplete callbacks</h3>
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="callbacks" @rows={{this.autocompleteCallbackRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Accessibility" @id="accessibility">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The default trigger is a button with aria-haspopup="listbox" and aria-expanded; the menu is a kit wu-autocomplete-list with role="option" items; aria-selected marks the highlighted option and aria-checked plus a check mark the current value. A custom trigger renders a kit wu-dropdown action menu with role="menuitem" items.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Filterable mode renders role="combobox" with aria-expanded, aria-controls and aria-autocomplete="list".</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Arrow keys move the highlight, Enter selects, Escape and Tab close; closing returns focus to the trigger. Escape is prevented and stopped at the menu, so a dialog underneath stays open.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The highlighted option's id is set as aria-activedescendant on the trigger, the filter input or the in-menu search.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="RTL" @id="rtl">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Placement is logical: start and end are resolved against the trigger's computed direction.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Verify with the Dir switch: the menu's edge alignment and the select arrow swap sides.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>
</WovenDocs::Page>
